Every command this build has, and which features it was compiled with.

⚠️ "This build" is the point. `cloud`, `migrate` and `backup` are optional features, so two binaries of the same version can have very different command sets — and nothing else tells you which one you have. PyPI shipped five releases with no cloud commands at all and nobody noticed, because every check anyone ran read `--version` and stopped.

`-q` has no effect: the list is the answer.

ⓘ Named `commands`; `surface` still works, because tooling calls it that.

Usage: evnx commands [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --compact
          One line instead of indented JSON. Requires `--format json` (or `--json`)

      --no-color
          Disable colored output

  -q, --quiet
          Print nothing on success. Findings, warnings, errors and requested data still print

  -v, --verbose
          Enable verbose output

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Output:
      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format. `json` is the whole command tree, for tooling.
          
          Versioned by a `schema` field, so the shape can change without breaking anyone. The plain output carries no such promise — do not parse it.
          
          [default: pretty]
          [possible values: pretty, json]

      --json
          The whole command tree as JSON, for tooling. Same as --format json.

Exit codes:
    0  Ran, nothing to report
    2  Could not run: usage, config, I/O, or refused before any change
  141  Output closed early (broken pipe)

Full guide: https://docs.evnx.dev/cli/commands/commands
